; Test: Cross-rule superiority
; Coverage: a different Rsd[q] rule (not the one that triggered) defeats the attacker

; r1 and r3 both support q. r2 attacks q.
; r1 is NOT superior to r2, but r3 IS.
; So the attacker r2 is defeated via r3, and +d q.
(given a)
(given b)
(normally r1 a q)
(normally r2 b (not q))
(normally r3 b q)
(prefer r3 r2)

; r3 > r2 defeats the attacker, even though r1 != r3
; EXPECT: +D a
; EXPECT: +d a
; EXPECT: +D b
; EXPECT: +d b
; EXPECT: +d q
; EXPECT: -d ~q
